Subject: [PATCH] Fix factual errors; turn three of them into jokes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Memorial corrections (real victims — fixed straight, no wordplay):
- Utøya: Sharidyn Svebakk-Bøhn was from Drammen, not Drøbak. Added the
  verified detail that she turned 14 two days before and it was her first
  camp.
- Tokyo sarin: replaced the unverifiable "Shizuka Itō, ехал на
  собеседование" with Kazumasa Takahashi, deputy stationmaster at
  Kasumigaseki, who picked up the punctured sarin packet off the floor.
- Stalker: Larisa Tarkovskaya died in 1998, twelve years after Tarkovsky,
  not "через год". Solonitsyn (the Writer) died of cancer at 47 — a real 47
  that lands on the game's central number.
- Fukushima seawall was 5.7m, not 10m. The true figure widens the gap the
  line is about.
- Radio song: 1941 → 2026 is 85 years, matching l13 (was "восемьдесят").

Errors played rather than silently fixed:
- .demiurge had "нехватает" written solid. The typo sat inside the passage
  about a creator who botched the world, so the fix is kept visible:
  Архивариус corrects it and notes "у него и пробела не хватило".
- l70 conflated two separate lost fortunes — the 1Feex address (79,957 BTC
  from the Mt.Gox theft, no hard drive) and James Howells' Newport landfill
  drive (8,000 BTC). Split back apart, with Архивариус admitting the merge:
  memory glues two losses into one bigger one.
- l31 credited "легче представить конец света" to Fisher. Fisher credited
  Jameson and Žižek; Žižek credited Jameson; Jameson said he heard it
  somewhere. The most-quoted line about capitalism is an orphan — so the
  café chalkboard carries it unsigned, "впервые правильно".

Build artifact patched directly (npm registry is 403ing the esbuild tarball
this session); extracted bundle passes node --check.

